quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  8,9,"And (remember) when you were calling upon your Lord for help, He responded to your supplication, (saying:) ‘I am going to reinforce you with a thousand angels coming in ranks upon ranks.’"
  8,10,"Allah did not make it but as good news (of victory), and that your hearts may feel peace through it. And victory comes only from Allah. Indeed, Allah is All-Mighty, All-Wise."
  8,11,"And (remember) when He caused drowsiness to overcome you (on the night before the battle) as (a feeling of) security from Him, and He sent down water upon you from the sky to purify you with it, and to remove from you Satan’s pollution (of suspicions), and to fortify your hearts and to make (your) steps firm and steady."
  8,12,"And (remember) when your Lord revealed to the angels: ‘I am with you; so make the believers stand firm. I shall cast fear into the hearts of the (invading) disbelievers. So, strike (them) above the necks and strike each of their fingertips (during the battle).’"
  8,13,"That is because they defied Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him). And whosoever defies Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), Allah is indeed severe in retribution."
  8,14,"That (punishment) is yours, so taste it! And (know) that for the disbelievers, there is the punishment of Hell (as well)."
  8,15,"O believers! When you encounter an army of disbelievers advancing for battle, do not turn your backs (in retreat) from them."
  8,16,"And whoever turns his back (to flee) from them on such a day, unless it is a diversion in the battle or a (strategic) withdrawal to join another troop, shall certainly earn the wrath of Allah. And his refuge shall be Hell, an evil destination!"
